    "text": "Figure 1a and Figure S2 (Supporting Information) show the fabrication process for the coiled PDA/CNT yarn (CPCY) that is the stretchable energy harvesting electrode in the CM-twistron harvester (Scheme 1b). A vertically-grown CNT forest was synthesized on a silicon wafer by using chemical vapor deposition (Figure S2a(i), Supporting Information).[29,30] Two CNT sheet layers were horizontally drawn from a side wall of this forest (Figure S2a(ii), Supporting Information), stacked together so they shared the same CNT alignment direction, and then twist inserted under mechanical load while one sheet-stack end was not torsionally tethered (Figure S2a(iii), Supporting Information). The non-tethering enables preparation of CNT yarn that has low density since it contains little yarn twist (Figure S2a(iv), Supporting Information).[26] This low-density CNT yarn was then immersed in a solution of dopamine and tris-HCl buffer to self-polymerize the dopamine while the PDA was inserted into the CNT yarn (Figure 1a). Figure 1b provides spectroscopic evidence that self-polymerization dopamine has been incorporated into the CNT yarn. The peaks at 1615, 1327, and 1028 cm $ ^{-1} $ correspond to catechol aromatic rings, methylene groups, and C–N stretching vibrations, respectively.[31–33] These functional groups within the PDA confer hydrophilicity to the CNT yarn in the cell growth medium, as shown in Figure 1b inset. The intrinsic contact angle measured on a flat PDA coated surface was 21.1° and 16.3° for advancing and receding angle, respectively. Due to the hydrophilicity of PDA and the porous structure of a CNT yarn, water wicks into the hydrophilic porous matrix resulting in fully wetting surface with 0° of water contact angle.[34] Scanning electron microscope (SEM) and energy dispersive spectrometer (EDS) images of the cross-section of PDA-incorporated CNT yarn (PDA/CNT yarn) show that the PDA is evenly incorporated within the CNT yarn (Figure 1c). The incorporated PDA remains in the CNT yarn when the much further twist needed to generate a fully coiled CPCY is provided (Figures S2b and S3, Supporting Information).",
